# E §3.1 step 1 and L §8.3 (tally 2.1.3, issue #60): a reality's files are reprinted and hashed "in the order of their
# full paths, compared by code point", and `reprint` names a loose file as `run` does, as given. b/m.tally and a/n.tally
# sort by full path as a/n.tally, b/m.tally, the other way from their base names (m.tally, n.tally): each section is
# named by its path, in that order, and the hash is the sha256 of n's canonical text, then m's. Was `--- m.tally`, then
# `--- n.tally`, and the hash of m's text, then n's (T's SR-4: 48 of the suite's sets).
=== options disk reprint
=== b/m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
